    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn Exceptional c.1805 Gate Lodge A Unique Piece Of Daingean's Built Heritage\n\nDNG Kelly Duncan is delighted to bring to the market The Gate Lodge, Molesworth Street, Daingean, an exceptionally characterful two-bedroom residence offering a rare opportunity to acquire an authentic piece of the town's built heritage.\n\nDating from circa 1805, this detached, single-storey former gate lodge is recorded on the National Inventory of Architectural Heritage and is intrinsically linked with the historic former barracks complex at Daingean. Today, the building survives as a wonderfully individual private residence, retaining the architectural character and atmosphere of its origins while providing comfortable and highly practical modern accommodation.\n\nExtending to approximately 65 m² (700 ft²), The Gate Lodge has been extensively cared for and refurbished and is presented in ready-to-occupy condition. Its modest footprint has been particularly well utilised, providing two bedrooms, two en-suite bathrooms, a dual-aspect sitting room and kitchen/dining room, together with a covered rear porch and separate external utility.\n\nAs a Protected Structure, the property is BER exempt, and its architectural heritage remains evident throughout. Vaulted ceilings, exposed timber beams, exposed Pollagh brickwork, a substantial brick fireplace with solid-fuel stove, traditional half-door and vintage-inspired bathroom fittings combine to create a home of genuine individuality.\n\nThe dual-aspect sitting room is particularly impressive, where a vaulted ceiling and exposed beams rise above a striking exposed Pollagh brick feature wall. A solid-fuel stove sits within a substantial brick fireplace beneath a heavy timber mantel, creating an inviting focal point to the room.\n\nThe adjoining kitchen/dining room continues the character of the house with a vaulted, beamed ceiling, exposed Pollagh brickwork and a fitted kitchen with integrated appliances. A serving hatch connects the kitchen with the sitting room, while a beautiful traditional half-door opens to the covered rear porch and gardens beyond.\n\nBoth bedrooms benefit from their own en-suite facilities. The front bedroom enjoys a dual aspect, while the rear bedroom features a vaulted ceiling, exposed timber beams and further exposed Pollagh brickwork. Modern conveniences including electric heating and USB charging points sit comfortably alongside the period detailing.\n\nThe historic character continues outside. The enclosed rear garden is principally laid to lawn with a concrete patio and pathways, while original stone walls associated with the historic complex form part of the boundary. Immediately outside the rear half-door is a covered porch with Chinese slate flooring, Belfast sink with running water and countertop space, together with a separately secured utility area.\n\nTo the front, wrought-iron railings and gated access frame the approach to the residence, while the wider setting is distinguished by the imposing historic limestone entrance associated with the former complex.\n\nThe Gate Lodge is not simply an alternative to a conventional two-bedroom home. It is an opportunity to become custodian of a distinctive piece of Daingean's architectural heritage, presented in a form that is comfortable, manageable and ready for immediate occupation.\n\nThe property occupies a highly convenient position on Molesworth Street in the heart of Daingean, an established heritage town in east County Offaly. Everyday amenities are readily accessible within the town, including shops, schools, sporting facilities and local services, while the surrounding road network provides convenient connections throughout the Midlands.\n\nDaingean is well positioned for access to Tullamore, Edenderry and Portarlington, making The Gate Lodge an appealing proposition for those seeking the character and atmosphere of a historic property while remaining within easy reach of larger employment, retail and transport centres.\n\nViewing Is Strictly By Appointment With Sole Selling Agents DNG Kelly Duncan who can be contacted on 057 93 25050.\n\nDNG Kelly Duncan Your Trusted Real Estate Partners."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.18m x 1.11m\nA solid timber entrance door with fanlight opens to the entrance hallway, which features a tiled floor, dado rail and exposed timber beams to the ceiling.\n\nSitting Room - 4.11m x 4.37m\nA characterful dual-aspect reception room with an impressive vaulted ceiling and exposed timber beams. A striking exposed Pollagh brick feature wall incorporates a substantial brick fireplace with heavy timber mantel, tiled/slate hearth and solid-fuel stove. A serving hatch connects directly with the kitchen, while the room also benefits from an electric heater.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 4.11m x 2.50m\nThe kitchen/dining room continues the character of the property with a vaulted ceiling, exposed timber beams and feature exposed Pollagh brickwork. Floor and eye-level fitted cabinetry provides ample storage and incorporates an integrated oven, hob and extractor fan, with a tiled splashback behind the hob and tiled upstand to the countertop. A serving hatch connects with the sitting room, while a traditional half-door provides access to the covered rear porch and garden. Finished with linoleum floor covering and an electric heater.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.23m x 3.99m\nA dual-aspect bedroom positioned to the front of the property, finished with ceiling coving and benefiting from ample sockets, USB charging points and an electric heater.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.76m x 1.84m\nThe dual-aspect en-suite features a tiled floor, half-tiled walls and a fully tiled wet area with electric pump shower. There is a wash-hand basin with vanity, toilet with high-level vintage-style cistern, fitted mirror and shaver socket. A vaulted ceiling with exposed timber beams adds further character, while an electric heater and electric heated towel rail provide additional comfort. Windows provide natural light and ventilation, complemented by an extractor fan.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.60m x 3.05m\nA rear-aspect bedroom featuring a vaulted ceiling with exposed timber beams and a particularly attractive exposed Pollagh brick feature wall. The room is complete with ample sockets, USB charging points and an electric heater.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.92m x 1.90m\nFinished with a tiled floor, half-tiled walls and a fully tiled wet area incorporating an electric pump shower. There is a wash-hand basin, toilet with high-level vintage-style cistern, electric heated towel rail and electric heater. A window provides natural light and ventilation, complemented by an extractor fan.\n\nRear Porch - 0.91m x 2.92m\nAccessed directly through the traditional half-door from the kitchen/dining room, the covered rear porch is finished with Chinese slate flooring and incorporates a Belfast sink with running water together with useful countertop workspace. Located off the porch is a secure external utility area providing dedicated space and provision for both a washing machine and tumble dryer.\n\n"
      },
